(a) Public property. No person shall park, store, leave, or permit the parking, storing, or leaving of any abandoned vehicle or any junked vehicle upon any public property within the corporate limits of the city for a period in excess of five days.
(b) Private property. No person shall park, store, leave or permit the parking, storing, or leaving, of any junked vehicle upon any private property within the city for a period of time in excess of 30 days; provided, however, this section shall not apply to the following:
(1) Any vehicle enclosed within a building on private property;
(2) Any vehicle suitably screened or enclosed in such a way on private property as to substantially prevent the vehicle from being viewed from any public street or highway; provided, further, however, if vegetation or landscaping plants are used for such screening, such vegetation or landscaping plants shall be kept trimmed and/or pruned in an orderly regular fashion;
(3) Any vehicle held by an automotive maintenance, repair, or salvage facility, or similar business enterprise, lawfully licensed by the city and property operated in an appropriate business zone, pursuant to the zoning laws of the city;
(4) Any vehicle in operable condition specifically adopted or designed for operation on raceways or drag strips; or
(5) Any vehicle retained by the owner for antique collection purposes and bearing a valid state antique license tag; in the event said vehicle is not in operable condition, it shall be enclosed or screened as provided in subsection (b)(2) of this section.
(c) Public nuisance. The presence of an abandoned vehicle or a junked vehicle or any parts of such a vehicle on private or public property is hereby declared a public nuisance which may be abated as such in accordance with the provisions of this article.
(Code 2011, § 3-3-4; Ord. No. 06-09-03, § 1, 11-14-2006)
